# B06: Streaming Log Aggregator & Latency Watermark Tracker (`LogAggregator`)

This module implements a high-throughput streaming log aggregator (`LogAggregator`) that summarizes incoming log severity levels (`1=Info, 2=Warn, 3=Error`) and request latencies (`latency_ms`) in real time.
Its `invariant` guarantees `error_count <= total_logs` and non-negative maximum latency, while `ensures` verifies monotonic counter increments after each ingested log entry.

```jenny
module log_aggregator

pub enum LogError {
    InvalidLevel,
    NegativeLatency,
}

pub struct LogAggregator {
    pub total_logs: usize = 0,
    pub warn_count: usize = 0,
    pub error_count: usize = 0,
    pub total_latency_ms: i64 = 0,
    pub max_latency_ms: i64 = 0,

    invariant {
        self.error_count <= self.total_logs
        self.warn_count <= self.total_logs
        self.total_latency_ms >= 0
        self.max_latency_ms >= 0
    }
}

impl LogAggregator {
    pub fn new() -> LogAggregator
        ensures result.total_logs == 0
        ensures result.max_latency_ms == 0

    pub fn ingest(mut self, level: i32, latency_ms: i64) -> void ! LogError
        requires level >= 1 && level <= 3 else LogError.InvalidLevel
        requires latency_ms >= 0 else LogError.NegativeLatency
        ensures self.total_logs == old(self.total_logs) + 1
        ensures self.total_latency_ms == old(self.total_latency_ms) + latency_ms
        ensures self.max_latency_ms >= latency_ms

    pub fn is_unhealthy(self, max_allowed_errors: usize) -> bool
        ensures result == (self.error_count > max_allowed_errors)
}

@example("EX-B06-01: streaming log ingestion and peak latency tracking") {
    var agg = LogAggregator.new()
    agg.ingest(1, 25)!
    agg.ingest(2, 120)!
    agg.ingest(3, 85)!
    assert(agg.total_logs == 3)
    assert(agg.warn_count == 1)
    assert(agg.error_count == 1)
    assert(agg.total_latency_ms == 230)
    assert(agg.max_latency_ms == 120)
    assert(!agg.is_unhealthy(2))
}

@example("EX-B06-02: reject invalid log level or negative latency") {
    var agg = LogAggregator.new()
    val err_lvl = agg.ingest(9, 10)
    assert(err_lvl is LogError.InvalidLevel)

    val err_lat = agg.ingest(1, -5)
    assert(err_lat is LogError.NegativeLatency)
}
```
